}
```
Problem mergeGeometries requires same attributes/index status. BoxGeometry and PlaneGeometry both indexed and have position, normal, uv. CapsuleGeometry indexed? likely. Torus etc all uv/normal. Should be compatible. Some Sprite excluded. MeshBasic face etc. Puddle plane has same. Great.
- Outline meshes are same material and renderOrder -1, merge with each other. Fine.
- `geo.applyMatrix4` updates normals with normal matrix.
- For sprite local pos: `obj.getWorldPosition(local); local.applyMatrix4(inv); clone.position.copy(local)`, but preserve scale maybe world scale could include parent. Builders sprites scale in local but group scale 1. In hero none. Use clone and apply inverse? Could just skip sprites in merged obstacles? They're glow niceties. Keep approximate local position by matrixWorld position; clone scale same. For track props no sprites except lamp glows; merging track with sprites: we'd keep 2 per segment -> 24 sprites =24 calls! Need handle those. Track lamps add glow sprite each; all share glowTex but each sprite material unique. To reduce, remove lamp glows or merge as Points? Simpler remove lamp glow sprites from roofProp; rely on emissive orb. Or skip `keepSprites` for track and drop. For obstacles, keep 1 glow each.
